{"term":"that","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:70bdd9f5bed54a695e","definition":"Introducing a clause that is the object of a verb, especially a reporting verb or verb expressing belief, knowledge, perception, etc.","example":"He told me that the book is a good read.","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3979d5fda069ac1c69","definition":"Introducing a clause that is the subject of a verb, especially the ‘be’ verb or a verb expressing judgement, opinion, etc.","example":"It is almost certain that she will come.","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:658fa345af0e931fb9","definition":"Introducing the complement of a mandative verb.","example":"I insist that you come.","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:91cd74ad70d54281d9","definition":"Introducing a clause that complements an adjective or passive participle.","example":"I'm sure that you are right.","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1e28f3a