.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3ab417f93e07b2b79f","definition":"Introducing a premise or supposition for consideration: seeing as; inasmuch as; given that; as would appear from the fact that.","example":"What are you mad, that you doe reaſon ſo?","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, poetic","register":"archaic, poetic","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5bda6972f67b6266a4","definition":"Introducing an exclamation expressing a desire or wish.","example":"Oh that spring would come!","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, poetic","register":"archaic, poetic","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7ae565fbffdffd3cfb","definition":"Introducing an exclamation expressing a strong emotion such as sadness or surprise.","example":"That men should behave in such a way!","pos":"conj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, poetic","register":"archaic, poetic","wordFamily":["that clause","that'd"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:33873a38ccc33dc382","definition":"The (thing, person, idea, etc) indicated or understood from context, especially if more remote physically, temporally or mentally than one designated as “this”, or if expressing distinction.","example":"That book is a good read. This one isn't.","pos":"det","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"demonstrative","register":"demonstrative","w